       still stubbed with no real [38;5;153mfetch[39m, as it is today.
     - Log [38;5;153m"Logging in:", username, userId[39m, never the password.
     - Return [38;5;153m{ success: true, user: username, userId }[39m.
     - If [38;5;153muserId[39m is missing, send [38;5;153muserId: null[39m rather than leaving the field out, so the server sees the same shape
       every time.
  2. [1mForm submit handler[0m
     - Read [38;5;153mlocalStorage.getItem("userId")[39m, which returns [38;5;153mnull[39m if it isn't set, and pass it as the third argument.
     - This change doesn't write anything to [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m. Whatever sets [38;5;153muserId[39m is outside this scope.
  3. [1mError handling:[0m a missing [38;5;153muserId[39m never blocks login. It just goes as [38;5;153mnull[39m.
  4. [1mTesting:[0m there's no test runner, and [38;5;153mapp.js[39m touches the DOM as soon as it loads. I'll check it by hand: load
     [38;5;153mindex.html[39m with [38;5;153muserId[39m set and with it unset, and confirm the logged payload and result. Adding a test setup would
     be a separate decision.
  5. [1mCaveat:[0m this [38;5;153muserId[39m comes from the client and can be spoofed, so the server shouldn't treat it as proof of who
